# Forest flying beetle (#330, D145): native 40x32 frames, facing right, redrawn 2026-11-26 after the author's photos of a
# beetle in flight: the two wing covers lifted apart, a long veined hindwing, a segmented belly, jointed legs and clubbed
# antennae. The body hitbox is x 10..31, y 17..31 (thorax, belly, head and legs); the wings, covers and antennae lie outside.
# fly1, fly2, fly3: the wingbeat (up, level, down; played 1 2 3 2); clap: the covers shut (the notice, drawn 3 px down);
# tip: covers open, head tipped down (the notice); brace, bright, white: the wind-up (shake + blink brace/bright, white last);
# dive: nose down, covers and hindwing swept back; dead: on its back, belly up, legs in the air, a wing flat on the floor (D101).
# Danger family (#236): the ground beetle's palette plus the wing membrane bc98a8, veined in the legs' 9a6070.
